    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40419" root="نقص" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاقِصٌ</span></b>  act. part. n. of 1. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِرْهَمٌ نَاقِضٌ</span> signifies <i>A
dirhem deficient in weight;</i> (Msb;) <i>light and
deficient:</i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُقَّصٌ</span> occurs as pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ناقص</span> thus
applied, agreeably with analogy. (Mgh.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
[Hence, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِعْلٌ نَاقِصٌ</span> meaning <i>An incomplete,</i>
i. e. <i>a non-attributive, verb:</i> opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِعْلٌ تَامٌّ</span>.]

